From: Chen Lin <chenlin@fnnas.com>
Subject: [PATCH] SDBM_File: use existing allocator declarations

sdbm.h already includes stdlib.h and declares the Perl allocators when
MYMALLOC is enabled. Redeclaring malloc/free with configured Malloc_t
can conflict with the system void pointer prototypes when Malloc_t is
char *. Remove the redundant declarations for both allocator modes.

Signed-off-by: Chen Lin <chenlin@fnnas.com>

--- a/ext/SDBM_File/sdbm.c
+++ b/ext/SDBM_File/sdbm.c
@@ -35,8 +35,6 @@
 extern "C" {
 #endif
 
-extern Malloc_t malloc(MEM_SIZE);
-extern Free_t free(Malloc_t);
 
 #ifdef __cplusplus
 }
